{"agent":"fleet-chorequeue","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"`_NOT_WITH_QUEUE` lists `message, keep, allow_dirty, allow_empty, branch`, but `--model` is also a landing-only flag (the non-queue branch passes it straight into `api.merge_item(..., model=a.get(\"model\", \"\") or \"\")`, and the `queue add` branch never uses it). The stated intent is that \"landing flags refused with --queue\", yet `ddflow merge --queue --model gpt-x <id>` passes the clash check (since `model` is not in the tuple), takes the `queue_add` path, and silently drops the requested model instead of returning the `queue.add` refusal that `--message`/`--branch`/etc. produce. Either `model` belongs in `_NOT_WITH_QUEUE` (so it is refused like the other landing flags) or the intent text is wrong; as written the two disagree and the flag is silently ignored.","digest":"a533ea171cb1643f","location":"ddflow/surfaces/declared/lifecycle_cli.py:_NOT_WITH_QUEUE","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/surfaces/declared/lifecycle_cli.py:_NOT_WITH_QUEUE"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"4/4 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":16307,"diff_sha":"449bf47d8c3a1397e713f53413b01d97ca1190c21359e4525bb035612fde2c37","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":288.9,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","output_digest":"11b8462a5a821cbc","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/DX-merge-queue-flag.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash.20261017T103953Z-50c0c079.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4],"reviewed_head":"bfa828b2591eddcaa218ad6b0ad2dc892a845a2f","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/surfaces/declared/lifecycle_cli.py:_NOT_WITH_QUEUE"],"tree_sha":"bfa828b2591e+