{"agent":"fleet-chorequeue","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"`_NOT_WITH_QUEUE` omits `model`, yet `model` is a landing-only flag: in the same function it is only ever forwarded to `api.merge_item(model=...)`, and the queue path calls `api.queue_add(repo, a[\"id\"], agent=agent)` without it. So `ddflow merge --queue --model opus <id>` passes the clash check (the list is `message, keep, allow_dirty, allow_empty, branch`) and silently enqueues, discarding the requested model with no refusal and no indication. This contradicts the change's own stated contract (\"landing flags refused with --queue\" / the constant's docstring \"What a landing flag means nothing for once the item is only being enqueued\") and the analogous handling of every other landing-only flag. Fix: add `\"model\"` to `_NOT_WITH_QUEUE` (or forward it), so the user gets the same refusal they get for `--message`/`--branch` instead of a silently no-op flag.","digest":"4c1a734bfcf16415","location":"ddflow/surfaces/declared/lifecycle_cli.py:391 (`_NOT_WITH_QUEUE` / `merge_call`)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/surfaces/declared/lifecycle_cli.py:391 (`_NOT_WITH_QUEUE` / `merge_call`)"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"The test runs the CLI `merge T1 --queue` first (which performs a real `queue add` for T1) and then, on the *same* repo and same item, calls the MCP tool with `{\"id\": \"T1\", \"queue\": True}`, asserting `mcp == cli`. The two bodies both carry the queue-entry fields `position`/`state`/`queued`, so equality only holds if enqueueing an already-queued item is a silent no-op returning the original entry. Given the stated semantics (\"enqueues the item (queue add)\", with a fresh add yielding `position == 1` in the sibling test), a perfectly reasonable implementation either appends a second entry (MCP returns `position: 2` while the CLI body has `position: 1`) or refuses the duplicate — in the second case `Server(...).handle(...)` returns a JSON-RPC `error` object, so `reply[\"result\"][\"content\"][0][\"text\"]` raises `KeyError`. Input demonstrating it: a repo where T1 was just enqueued by the preceding CLI call, then the MCP call above. The comparison is between two different queue states, so it does not establish the claimed \"CLI and MCP bodies are equal\" property and will fail (or be vacuous, if the MCP call is merely deduplicated) for a correct non-idempotent `merge --queue`; use a separate repo or a second fresh item for the MCP leg.","digest":"b3facebfcc5a0815","location":"tests/test_merge_queue.py::test_merge_queue_cli_and_mcp_bodies_are_equal","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_merge_queue.py::test_merge_queue_cli_and_mcp_bodies_are_equal"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"4/4 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":16307,"diff_sha":"449bf47d8c3a1397e713f53413b01d97ca1190c21359e4525bb035612fde2c37","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":376.0,"family":"deepseek","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","output_digest":"0fc537f2687b5873","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/DX-merge-queue-flag.critic.lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash.20261017T104442Z-a2ff865c.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4],"reviewed_head":"bfa828b2591eddcaa218ad6b0ad2dc892a845a2f","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/surfaces/declared/lifecycle_cli.py:391 (`_NOT_WITH_QUEUE` / `merge_call`)","tests/test_merge_queue.py::test_merge_queue_cli_and_mcp_bodies_are_equal"],"tree_sha":"bfa828b2591e+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"critic","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"e5189ba818a27b81411510dc7","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":74397,"schema":1,"subject":"DX-merge-queue-flag","ts":"2026-10-17T10:50:59.067021Z"}
